{%- comment -%}
  Florista footer — decided with the owner on 2026-08-20, see docs/design-log.md.
  Revised 2026-08-21: logo moved to the foot of the footer and centred, newsletter sign-up added,
  and the delivery-areas column removed — all three asked for by the owner directly. The seven cities
  are still edited in theme settings (`delivery_areas`); the /pages/delivery link in the shop
  column is now the only footer route to them.

  Contact-first flat stack, chosen over a nav-first order and an accordion: flowers are an
  urgency purchase, so "can I reach you, are you open" has to be readable without a tap. Order,
  mobile:

    1. Contact + hours       — phone (tap-to-call), email, address, two FIXED hour lines.
                                Never "open now": the Friday/erev-chag close is a moving target
                                and a computed line would be wrong the moment it drifts, same
                                reasoning as the announcement bar's cutoff text.
    2. Shop links            — the header's five categories, PLUS the four info links
                                (delivery/about/blog/privacy) that live in the header's mobile
                                drawer only. That drawer disappears at 768px, so above that width
                                this is currently the ONLY path to those pages — not decoration.
    3. Newsletter            — one email field and one button. Last of the three blocks because
                                it is the only one asking the customer for something rather than
                                giving them something.
    4. Wordmark + tagline    — the header carries the mark only; the wordmark lives here. It sat
                                at the top of the stack until 2026-08-21; it now closes the
                                footer, centred and full-width, so the page signs off with the
                                brand instead of opening a utility block with it.
    5. Bottom bar            — copyright, centred under the centred wordmark.

  Desktop: the three utility blocks become one row of columns — contact · links · newsletter —
  with the wordmark spanning the full width beneath them. No accordion, nothing hidden.

  Background is the subtle surface token, not wine. "The flowers are the colour, the interface
  is not" (florista-tokens.css) — a full-bleed brand-colour footer is exactly the large-background
  use the token file rules out; wine stays reserved for the links, icons and the sign-up button.

  Top edge (added 2026-08-25, from a reference the owner brought): the hard border became an organic
  two-layer "hills" divider. The front layer is the footer's own sand, so the shape flows into
  the body with no seam; the back layer is the same sand at partial opacity, which over the
  ivory page ground reads as a paler dune behind it. The sky between the hills is transparent —
  whatever section sits above shows through, so the divider works on any page.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'florista-footer.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- liquid
  # Same menu + same five-collection fallback as the header, so the two surfaces cannot drift
  # apart. See florista-header.liquid for why the fallback exists at all.
  assign menu = linklists[section.settings.menu]
  assign titles = ''
  assign urls = ''

  if menu.links.size > 0
    for link in menu.links
      # Dropdown groups (a parent whose link is '#', e.g. «מוצרים נלווים») stay out of the
      # footer: The owner's call, 2026-08-29 — the footer lists pages, not the nav's fold-out
      # structure, and a '#' link here would go nowhere.
      if link.url == '#'
        continue
      endif
      assign titles = titles | append: link.title | append: '|'
      assign urls = urls | append: link.url | append: '|'
    endfor
  else
    assign titles = 'זרי פרחים|סידורים בקופסה|סידורים בסלסלה|צמחים|זרי כלה|חתונות|'
    assign urls = '/collections/bouquets|/collections/box-arrangements|/collections/basket-arrangements|/collections/plants|/pages/bridal|/pages/weddings|'
  endif

  # The info pages the header's mobile drawer carries but desktop cannot reach at all.
  # Fixed, not menu-driven — see the comment block above. The privacy policy joins them last
  # (added 2026-08-22, asked for by the owner): it is the one link here nobody browses to, so it sits
  # at the end of the list where a reader looks for it rather than competing with the shop links.
  # Since 2026-09-05 it points at Shopify's own policy slot, /policies/privacy-policy — the owner
  # wants ONE policy page on the site, and that is the one checkout and the cookie banner link
  # to. The theme page /pages/privacy-policy is deleted and redirects there.
  # The terms of use (2026-09-10) live in the same slot, /policies/terms-of-service, for the same
  # reason: checkout links the terms from there, and the owner wants each policy in exactly one place.
  # The cancellations-and-returns policy (2026-09-12) sits between them: /policies/refund-policy
  # existed since 2026-09-10 but nothing on the site linked it, and Google's listing rules want
  # the return policy reachable from the store. Its display name is the owner's, not Shopify's fixed
  # "מדיניות החזרים כספיים" — theme.liquid retitles that page to match.
  assign titles = titles | append: 'משלוחים|אודותינו|בלוג|תנאי שימוש|מדיניות הביטולים וההחזרות|מדיניות פרטיות'
  assign urls = urls | append: '/pages/delivery|/pages/about|/blogs/flora|/policies/terms-of-service|/policies/refund-policy|/policies/privacy-policy'

  assign titles = titles | split: '|'
  assign urls = urls | split: '|'

  assign phone_display = settings.phone_display | default: '054-2270287'
  assign phone_e164 = settings.phone_e164 | default: '+972542270287'
  assign email = settings.email | default: 'floristahaifa@gmail.com'
  assign address = settings.address | default: 'חניתה 34, נווה שאנן, חיפה'
  assign hours_weekday = settings.hours_weekday | default: 'ראשון–חמישי: 08:00–20:00'
  assign hours_friday = settings.hours_friday | default: 'שישי וערבי חג: 08:00 עד 30 דק׳ לפני כניסת השבת'
  assign news_placeholder = section.settings.newsletter_placeholder | default: 'הירשמו לניוזלטר שלנו לקבלת מבצעים'
  assign news_button = section.settings.newsletter_button | default: 'הרשמה'
  assign news_success = section.settings.newsletter_success | default: 'תודה! נרשמתם לניוזלטר.'
  assign news_id = 'ff-newsletter-' | append: section.id
-%}

<footer class="ff-footer">
  <div class="ff-ground">
  <div class="ff-inner">
    <div class="ff-contact">
      <a class="ff-contact-line ff-contact-link" href="tel:{{ phone_e164 }}">
        {%- render 'icon-phone' -%}
        <span dir="ltr">{{ phone_display }}</span>
      </a>
      <a class="ff-contact-line ff-contact-link" href="mailto:{{ email }}">
        {%- render 'icon-mail' -%}
        <span dir="ltr">{{ email }}</span>
      </a>
      <p class="ff-contact-line">
        {%- render 'icon-pin' -%}
        <span>{{ address }}</span>
      </p>
      <p class="ff-contact-line ff-hours">
        {%- render 'icon-clock' -%}
        <span>{{ hours_weekday }}<br>{{ hours_friday }}</span>
      </p>
    </div>

    <nav class="ff-links" aria-label="ניווט בפוטר">
      <ul class="ff-links-list">
        {%- for url in urls -%}
          <li>
            <a class="ff-links-link" href="{{ url }}"{% if request.path == url %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>
              {{ titles[forloop.index0] }}
            </a>
          </li>
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <div class="ff-newsletter">
      {%- comment -%}
        Shopify's own customer form: an accepted submission creates a customer tagged
        `newsletter`, which is what every email app on the store reads. No third-party embed,
        no JS — the field works with the tab key and with scripting off.

        The placeholder is the only visible prompt, so the <label> is real and visually hidden
        rather than dropped: a placeholder disappears the moment the field is typed into, and a
        screen reader gets nothing from it at all.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- form 'customer', class: 'ff-newsletter-form' -%}
        <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="newsletter">
        <label class="ff-sr-only" for="{{ news_id }}">{{ news_placeholder }}</label>

        <div class="ff-newsletter-field">
          <input
            id="{{ news_id }}"
            class="ff-newsletter-input"
            type="email"
            name="contact[email]"
            placeholder="{{ news_placeholder }}"
            autocomplete="email"
            autocorrect="off"
            autocapitalize="off"
            spellcheck="false"
            required
            {% if form.errors %}
              aria-invalid="true"
              aria-describedby="{{ news_id }}-error"
            {% endif %}
          >
          <button class="ff-newsletter-submit" type="submit" name="commit">{{ news_button }}</button>
        </div>

        {%- if form.errors -%}
          <p class="ff-newsletter-message ff-newsletter-error" id="{{ news_id }}-error" role="alert">
            {{ form.errors.translated_fields.email | capitalize }} {{ form.errors.messages.email }}
          </p>
        {%- elsif form.posted_successfully? -%}
          <p class="ff-newsletter-message ff-newsletter-success" role="status">{{ news_success }}</p>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endform -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="ff-brand">
    <img
      class="ff-logo"
      src="{{ 'florista-logo-horizontal-rtl.svg' | asset_url }}"
      alt="פלוריסטה"
      width="160"
      height="55"
      loading="lazy"
    >
    <p class="ff-tagline">חנות פרחים בחיפה</p>
  </div>

  <div class="ff-bottom">
    {%- comment -%}
      dir="ltr" is load-bearing, same reasoning as the header's phone number: an RTL paragraph
      reorders "© 2026 florista" into "florista 2026 ©" because the brand name is the only
      strongly-directional run in the line.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p dir="ltr">© {{ 'now' | date: '%Y' }} florista</p>
  </div>
  </div>
</footer>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Florista footer",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "link_list",
      "id": "menu",
      "label": "תפריט קטגוריות",
      "default": "main-menu",
      "info": "אותו תפריט כמו בכותרת. אם ריק, יוצגו חמש הקטגוריות כברירת מחדל. ארבעת קישורי המידע (משלוחים/אודותינו/בלוג/מדיניות פרטיות) קבועים ומתווספים תמיד."
    },
    {
      "type": "header",
      "content": "ניוזלטר"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "newsletter_placeholder",
      "label": "טקסט מציין מקום בשדה המייל",
      "default": "הירשמו לניוזלטר שלנו לקבלת מבצעים"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "newsletter_button",
      "label": "טקסט הכפתור",
      "default": "הרשמה"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "newsletter_success",
      "label": "הודעה לאחר הרשמה מוצלחת",
      "default": "תודה! נרשמתם לניוזלטר."
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
